! mcp_bootstrap_p142.strap -- the TENTACLE-PARAMETER loop, the PP
! interrupt return (M PP1) and the entry to the backup-buffer scan
! (JMPP1), printed page 142.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.149, header READ and not assumed:
! "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD ID FA000097
!  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  142", and the column-heading
! row's own "LOCATION 217245" names the page's first word.
!
! FIFTY-SIX PRINTED LINES, FIFTY-TWO OF WHICH EMIT BITS.  Lines 52,
! 53, 54 and 55 are COMMENT CARDS -- no LOCATION, no BINARY OUTPUT;
! line 54 carries "*****CHECK FOR OP, AD, USA, OR DS IN BACKUP
! BUFFER*****" and the other three are blank but for the "-" in the
! flag column.  Everything else is code: no DRZ, no XW, no SYN, no
! reservation, and no SLC.
!
! CARD SERIALS FA000097 (line 1) to FA000148 (line 56) -- fifty-two
! serials for fifty-six lines, read at 400 dpi off the right-hand
! column, so nothing fell off the top or the bottom of the render.
! Four pairs of lines share a card by the serial column -- 20/21,
! 23/24, 25/26 and 47/48 -- while lines 22, 27 and 49 carry the next
! serial in sequence, so the run FA000097..FA000148 is continuous
! with exactly four duplicates.  ONLY 20/21 IS EXPLAINED: it is
! "SIC,JMPP2" and its branch, the semicolon double-statement card
! printed pp.127, 131 and 136 also carry.  The other three pairs are
! not SIC/branch pairs and no reason is offered for them here.  The
! load-bearing claim is only that nothing fell off the top or the
! bottom of the render.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! BOTH JOINS ARE MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE BACKWARD JOIN IS READ OFF THE PREVIOUS PAGE ITSELF. <<<
! This page prints no SLC, so the "SLC,(8)217245.0" written below is
! an ASSERTION as far as this deck's own checks go (a hard SLC
! cannot disagree with the arriving counter -- docs/transcription_
! workflow.md, "A HARD SLC CANNOT DISAGREE WITH THE ARRIVING
! COUNTER").  It is nevertheless MEASURED, by rendering PDF p.148 at
! 400 dpi: printed p.141 has FIFTY lines, not fifty-six, and its
! last is
!     50*  217244.00   000000.00 82  004066.60 50
!          L(BU,4),0.0($2),-19
! a VFL FULL WORD at 217244.00, which occupies 217244.00 and
! 217244.40 and leaves the counter at exactly 217245.00.  That is
! this page's own line 1, and it is also what the heading row's
! "LOCATION 217245" field prints.  Three readings, one value.
!
! >>> THE FORWARD JOIN HAS TWO WITNESSES. <<<  Line 56 is a VFL full
! word at 217306.40, so it occupies 217306.40 and 217307.00 and the
! counter leaves at 217307.40.
!   (a) The volume OCR of printed p.143 (PDF p.150) reads its line 1
!       as "1* 217307.4C * 720CCC.CO 80 405000.C3 7C
!       CTICOO1(BU,5),(2)11101" -- 217307.40, exactly where this
!       page's counter arrives, and carrying the same bare "*" in
!       the location column that lines 1, 19 and 37 carry here.
!   (b) p.143's line 2 is "2* 21731C.40 217310.74 C2  JMPP2  BRZ,$
!       - SIC INTO HERE", which is the DEFINING card for JMPP2 at
!       217310.40 -- the address this page's line 20 SICs to.  An
!       off-page reading of both the address and the spelling.
!
! TAIL SCOPE.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the
! origin and pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the TAIL,(2)G block that printed p.2
! opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed with "UNTAIL,(2)".  Names
! here may legitimately repeat names from pp.2-98 at other
! addresses; none of this page's six does.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE CONTAINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 1-15   THE TENTACLE-PARAMETER LOOP.  $0 is set to the
!              left-zeros count ($L), doubled and complemented to
!              give "-N IN $0" (line 3's comment); line 4 multiplies
!              M PRM QK by it with a -19 bit offset; line 5 saves
!              the transmit control out of M R 5.  Line 6's
!              CM1111(BU,1),.4($2) "SETs USER TO MCP", lines 7-8
!              plant $2 in M CR ("-SET K IN MCR") and in MR3 AD,
!              lines 9-10 clear and step it.  M UP 5A (line 11) is
!              the loop: load a parameter with progressive indexing
!              and refill ("L(V+ICR)"), store it with progressive
!              indexing into the tentacle ("-PARAM. TO TENT."),
!              count back on CB until "-PARAM FINISHED".  Line 14
!              saves the unprime control and line 15 enters M TC 1.
! Lines 16-17  M B1: store STIC into the saved-IC slot and branch to
!              K SUPP.
! Lines 18-21  M PP1, the PP-level entry: clear M CR, step index 9,
!              then SIC,JMPP2 / B,JMPP1 -- "-CHECK FOR OP, AD, USA,
!              DS" -- the SIC/branch pair on one card.
! Lines 22-32  the AUTO-STACK path.  If S AS is on, return to the PP
!              at C RET BU ("-RETURN TO PP IF HE IS AUTO STACKED");
!              otherwise load index 13, branch on index-value-zero
!              to RSIOTT, and (lines 25-32) call K SERCH with a
!              return address in $1, then transmit 30 words of
!              S LR BU into S LR PP, set two bits and go to K INTTY.
! Lines 33-40  RSIOTT, the same shape for the SUPPRESSED-I/O bit:
!              test S SIO, read S QK, "-NO PP INTERRUPTS STACKED"
!              branches to C RET BU, otherwise 30 words are moved
!              and control goes to K UNSTC.
! Lines 41-51  C RET BU, the return to the backup level: 29 words
!              this time, S L and S LR BU+9.0 toggled, "-CHECK FOR
!              TS, EXE" through J TSEXE, S LR BU restated as a VF,
!              S IC BU loaded, the save-value-address of $+2,
!              "-RESTORE $MR" out of S LR BU+1.0, three words
!              transmitted, and line 51's "BE,$" (Branch Enabled to
!              itself) as the wait.
! Lines 52-55  comment cards; line 54 heads the next section.
! Line 56      JMPP1: "LF(BU,5),SLRBU+8.15  -PICK UP OP, USA, EXE,
!              DS" -- the first word of the backup-buffer scan whose
!              body is printed p.143.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SIX NAMES THIS PAGE DEFINES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   M UP 5A  217253.00     M B1    217256.40     M PP1   217260.00
!   RSIOTT   217271.40     C RET BU 217277.40    JMPP1   217306.40
!
! TWO OF THE SIX HAVE AN INDEPENDENT OFF-PAGE WITNESS, both on
! printed p.141, read from the volume OCR of a page this deck does
! not transcribe:
!   M B1   217256.40   p.141 line 49, "217243.00  000000.11 82
!                      217256.74 02   BB,.9($2),M B1" -- and that
!                      row is also on the 400 dpi render of PDF
!                      p.148 made for the backward join, so the
!                      address was read from the image and not only
!                      from the OCR.  0o74 has bit 18 set, so .40.
!   M PP1  217260.00   p.141 line 44, "217240.00  217260.31 46
!                      BXVZZ,M PP 1".  0o31 has bit 18 clear, so
!                      .00.  Printed there WITH a blank before the
!                      1, here without; STRAP ignores blanks in a
!                      name.
! THE OTHER FOUR -- M UP 5A, RSIOTT, C RET BU and JMPP1 -- have no
! off-page witness at all.  Each LOCATION is pinned twice on this
! page (M UP 5A by line 11's own location and line 13's CB;
! RSIOTT by line 33 and the branches on lines 24 and 27; C RET BU by
! line 41 and the branch-on-bit targets on lines 22, 33 and 35;
! JMPP1 by line 56 and line 21's branch), so the ADDRESSES are safe.
! THE SPELLINGS REST ON INK:
!   "RSIOTT" -- the fourth glyph is a round open bowl.  Read O, not
!   C, on the asymmetry rule (dropout opens a closed glyph and never
!   closes an open one) and because the row it labels tests S SIO,
!   whose own O two inches to the right is printed the same way.  No
!   manual and no other page carries the name; recorded as a
!   reading, not a proof.
!   "C RET BU" -- read C.  The MCP's C-family names are attested
!   elsewhere in the volume (C WAIT and C NOWAT at 216226.40 and
!   216225.00), and this page prints the name four times (line 41's
!   NAME column and lines 22, 33, 35 as "CRETBU"), always with the
!   same glyph.
!   "M UP 5A" -- the last two characters are 5 and A, read at 1200
!   dpi; the A has a clear apex.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> "M PRM GK" IS "M PRM QK", AND THE PAGE'S OWN INK SETTLES IT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 4's second operand was read "M PRM GK" on the first pass.  At
! 1800 dpi the glyph is a round bowl with a short DIAGONAL stroke at
! the LOWER RIGHT, crossing the bowl and running outside it -- which
! is the same glyph line 34 prints in "S QK" on this page, and not
! a G (a G's bar is at mid height, horizontal, and runs inward).
! Two further readings agree: printed p.120 line 6 is the DEFINING
! card, "M PRM QK DRZ", already landed as MPRMQK in decks/mcp_
! bootstrap_p119.strap, and the volume OCR of printed p.141 line 42
! reads "LV,1,MPRMQK".  THE DECK FOLLOWS p.119/p.120's SPELLING AND
! SAYS SO.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE BYTE COLUMN: THIS PAGE PRINTS A LOW-NIBBLE 0 AS AN OPEN C,
! AND LINES 42 AND 43 PROVE IT ON ROWS WHOSE VALUE IS CERTAIN
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 4 and 12 print their trailing hex nibble OPEN -- "9C" and
! "DC" to the eye at 900, 1200 and 1800 dpi.  Both are read here as
! 0, and the evidence is NOT the usual adjacent-octal-field argument
! (which docs/transcription_workflow.md calls necessary but not
! sufficient, and which on line 4 came out differently at 1200 dpi
! than at 1800 dpi).  It is this:
!
!   (a) LINES 42 AND 43 PRINT "001000.CC FC" WHERE THE VALUE IS
!       CERTAIN.  They are "CM0000(BU,1),S L" and "CM0000(BU,1),
!       SLRBU+9.0" -- the SAME TWO STATEMENTS as lines 31 and 30,
!       and as lines 39 and 38, which print a CLOSED "F0" in the
!       identical column.  All six assemble to F0 and all six
!       !CHECKs below pass.  So this page demonstrably opens the
!       byte's low-nibble 0, in exactly that column, on rows where
!       0 is established four other ways.  It is per-CHARACTER, not
!       a band failure: line 48's "D0" eight rows later prints
!       closed.
!   (b) WHAT PRODUCED THEM.  The low nibble of a VFL full word is
!       i2, the offset index from the OF7(I') operand (vflAddrOf:
!       w[3:0], IBM 60-63).  Line 12's "ST(V+I)(BU,32),.32($2)" has
!       NO offset operand at all, so i2 is 0; its twin line 11,
!       "L(V+ICR)(BU,32),.32($3)", is the same shape and prints a
!       closed 0.  Line 4's offset operand is the literal -19 and
!       carries no index, so i2 is 0 there too.
! Recorded as 90 and D0.  The raw ink reads 9C and DC and that is
! written here rather than quietly dropped.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE ASSEMBLER GAP: "M-" ON A VFL OPERATION (LINE 4) <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 4 is printed "M-(BU,19),M PRM QK,-19" -- read at 1800 dpi,
! and the "M-" is unambiguous.  strap_asm raises KeyError 'M-' out
! of VFL_INT_CODES, which ABORTS the whole assembly, so leaving the
! printed form in would check NOTHING on this page.  The deck
! therefore writes "M+N(BU,19),MPRMQK,-19".
!
! MEASURED, and that is all that is claimed for it:
!     M+N(BU,19),MPRMQK,-19  ->  215640.00 80  023066.70 90
! which is the printed row (see the byte note above).  The other
! twenty-eight accepted VFL spellings were tried and none of them
! produces that word:  M+ gives .60 90, M+1 gives .62 B0, M-1 gives
! .72 B0, -MG gives .72 10, "-" alone gives .70 10.
!
! >>> THIS IS A SUBSTITUTION AND IT IS THE WEAKEST !CHECK ON THE
! PAGE. <<<  The operation is substituted AND the row's final nibble
! is read against contrary ink, so its check verifies rather less
! than the other fifty-one do.  WHAT THE ROW DOES ESTABLISH ON ITS
! OWN, with no circularity, is the OCTAL FIELD "023066.70": that
! field is clean ink, and 0o70 against M+'s 0o60 is exactly the
! invert-sign bit -- the same 0o10 that separates M-1 (.72) from
! M+1 (.62) and "-" (.70) from "+" (.60).  So the page independently
! confirms that line 4 is a NEGATED multiply, whatever is written in
! the deck to get it there.
!
! THE GAP IS REAL AND IT IS A FINDING.  strap/opcodes.py's
! VFL_INT_WRITTEN_MINUS deliberately omits "M-" with the note "M-
! AND M-MG REMAIN DELIBERATELY ABSENT.  Nothing in the corpus spells
! either of them on a VFL operation."  THIS PAGE SPELLS IT: "M-" on
! a VFL operation carrying a VFL data description "(BU,19)", which
! is precisely the standard that file applied when it admitted "M-1"
! (MCP printed p.92 line 27) and "-MG" (Reference Manual printed
! p.61, Figure 12).  printed p.142 line 4 is the witness that would
! admit M-.  Not changed here -- this deck touches nothing under
! strap/.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS.  WHAT IS READ AND WHAT IS CONVENTION
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The distinction was MEASURED on this page's own rows rather than
! assumed: each SYN below was re-assembled with its bit offset set
! to .0, .04 and .40 and the printed half word compared.
!
! FULLY OBSERVED (the bit offset lands in a printed address field):
!   MPRMQK  line 4 is a VFL operand, so the whole 24-bit address
!           prints -- .04 would print "215640.04".  .00 is READ.
!   STIC    line 16, the same -- "215265.00 80".  .00 is READ.
!   SLRBU   line 46 is "VF,SLRBU", which prints the 24-bit value
!           and its sign -- .04 would print "215324.04+".  READ.
!   SL      line 31/39/42 are VFL operands printing "215001.04", so
!           bit 4 is READ, not conventional.
!   SAS/SSIO  lines 22 and 33 are Branch on Bit and print the bit
!           address directly, 0o31 = 25 and 0o75 = 61.
!
! HALF WORD ONLY (bit 18 shows, bits 19-23 are swallowed by the
! operation or register field, so ".0" below is a CONVENTION and no
! !CHECK here can test it -- docs/transcription_workflow.md, "WHAT
! THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE", item 1):
!   MR5, MCR, MR3AD, SICBU, SLRPP  -- index and Transmit operands.
!           Measured: setting MCR to .04 changes nothing; setting it
!           to .40 turns line 7's ".05" into ".45", which WOULD
!           fail, so the half word itself is checked.
!   MTC1, KSUPP, JMPP2, KSERCH, KINTTY, KUNSTC, JTSEXE -- branch and
!           SIC targets.  The ".40" values are READ (bit 18 set in
!           the printed octal pair: 0o50 and 0o74 mean .40, 0o10 and
!           0o34 mean .00); the bits below are convention.
!
! MPRMQK  215640.00  LANDED as MPRMQK by decks/mcp_bootstrap_p119.
!                    strap from printed p.120 line 6's defining card
!                    "M PRM QK DRZ".  See the Q note above.
MPRMQK  SYN, (8)215640.0
! MR5     215645.00  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p119.strap, from
!                    printed p.120 line 12 "M R 5 DRZ".  The volume
!                    OCR carries that defining card, "1* 215645.00
!                    M R 5 DRZ(BU,64),(1)".  Lines 5 and 14 print
!                    215645.06 and 215645.07 -- 2*3 and 2*3+1 for
!                    register $3, which is the whole octal pair.
MR5     SYN, (8)215645.0
! MCR     215636.00  The volume OCR carries the defining card,
!                    "2* 215636.00  215016.00+  M CR  XS IPL IN
!                    -CURRENT TENTACLE TABLE ADDRESS".  Lines 7 and
!                    18 print 215636.05 and 215636.22.
MCR     SYN, (8)215636.0
! MR3AD   215546.00  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p117.strap line 42
!                    "MR3 AD"; p.118's !SYM puts it here.  The
!                    volume OCR carries the defining card,
!                    "25* 215546.00  00.+  M R 3AD  VF,0.0".
MR3AD   SYN, (8)215546.0
! MTC1    215546.40  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p118.strap !SYM.
!                    The volume OCR carries the defining card,
!                    "26* 215546.40 *  215547.10 06  M TC 1
!                    BUSAZ,$+.32".  Line 15 prints 215546.50, and
!                    0o50 has bit 18 set, so .40 is READ.
MTC1    SYN, (8)215546.40
! STIC    215265.00  LANDED by p110, p111, p112, p118, p128 and
!                    p136, and named in C22-6728's prose ("the saved
!                    IC is stored in STIC"), which is what settles
!                    the last letter as C.  Line 16 prints
!                    "215265.00 80" -- a VFL operand, so READ.
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0
! KSUPP   216242.00  The volume OCR carries the defining card,
!                    "2* 216242.00  216246.70 00  K SUPP
!                    NOP,K COMM R".  Line 17 prints 216242.10.
KSUPP   SYN, (8)216242.0
! JMPP2   217310.40  The DEFINING card is printed p.143 line 2, in
!                    the volume OCR as "2* 21731C.40  217310.74 C2
!                    JMPP2  BRZ,$  - SIC INTO HERE".  Line 20 here
!                    prints "217310.40 80"; SIC prints its operand's
!                    half word, and 0o40 is bit 18 set.
JMPP2   SYN, (8)217310.40
! KSERCH  222020.00  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p127.strap.  The
!                    volume OCR carries the defining card,
!                    "5* 222020.00  215021.23 01  K SERCH
!                    LVI,9,S PROG S".  Line 26 prints 222020.10.
KSERCH  SYN, (8)222020.0
! KINTTY  216010.40  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p123.strap !SYM.
!                    The volume OCR carries the defining card at
!                    216010.40 with "K INT TY" in the NAME column,
!                    and an off-page reference "220361.00
!                    000000.31 89  216010.74 02  BB,S AS($9),
!                    K INT TY".  Line 32 prints 216010.50 -- 0o50,
!                    bit 18 set, so .40 is READ.
KINTTY  SYN, (8)216010.40
! KUNSTC  222037.00  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p123.strap and
!                    p127.  The volume OCR carries an off-page
!                    reference, "216010.00  222037.10 00  K NENTY
!                    B,K UNSTC  -NOT FOUND RETURN".  Line 40 prints
!                    222037.10.
KUNSTC  SYN, (8)222037.0
! JTSEXE  217316.00  The volume OCR carries the DEFINING card,
!                    "15* 217316.00  000000.36 31  JTSEXE
!                    LV,$15,0.0($1)  -ADDRESS OF BUFFER", and an
!                    off-page reference "217200.40  217316.10 00
!                    B,JTSEXE".  Line 45 prints 217316.10.
JTSEXE  SYN, (8)217316.0
! SLRBU   215324.00  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p117.strap line 28
!                    and p.116's !SYM.  The volume OCR carries the
!                    defining card, "21* 215324.00 *  000035.00
!                    S LR BU  DRZ(BU,64),(29)".  FULLY OBSERVED
!                    here by line 46's VF.
SLRBU   SYN, (8)215324.0
! SLRPP   215266.00  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p116.strap line 18
!                    defines it; p123/p127/p134 carry it.  The
!                    volume OCR's defining card is "1* 215266.00 *
!                    000035.00  S LR PP  DRZ(BU,64),(29)".  Lines 29
!                    and 37 print 215266.36; half word only --
!                    measured, .04 changes nothing and .40 prints
!                    .76.
SLRPP   SYN, (8)215266.0
! SICBU   215361.00  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p116.strap !SYM and
!                    p127/p132.  The volume OCR carries the defining
!                    card, "24* 215361.00  000000.00 F  S IC BU
!                    VF,0", and off-page references at 216223.40 and
!                    216732.40.  Line 47 prints 215361.02 -- 2*1 for
!                    register 1, half word only.
SICBU   SYN, (8)215361.0
! SCOMRG  215001.00  LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap line 8
!                    ("S COM RG XW,(8)520000.").  Carried only so
!                    that S L can be written the way p.103 writes
!                    it.
SCOMRG  SYN, (8)215001.0
! SL      215001.04  LANDED, p.103 line 14, "S L SYN(BU,1),
!                    S COM RG + 0.04", and already used this way by
!                    decks/mcp_bootstrap_p136.strap.  Lines 31, 39
!                    and 42 are VFL operands printing "215001.04",
!                    so bit 4 is READ.
!                    >>> THE PAGE SPELLS IT BOTH WAYS. <<<  Line 31
!                    and line 39 print "SL"; line 42 prints "S L"
!                    with the blank.  The deck keeps both forms
!                    exactly as printed -- STRAP ignores blanks in a
!                    name and strap_asm resolves them to the same
!                    symbol (all three rows pass).
SL      SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+0.04
! SAS     .25        LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p109.strap line 8
!                    "-AUTO STACK STATUS".  Line 22 prints
!                    000000.31, 0o31 = 25, fully observed.
SAS     SYN(BU,1), .25
! SSIO    .61        LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p109.strap line 10
!                    "-SUPPRESSED MODE STATUS".  Line 33 prints
!                    000000.75, 0o75 = 61, fully observed.
SSIO    SYN(BU,1), .61
! SQK     .32        LANDED, decks/mcp_bootstrap_p109.strap line 9
!                    (no comment printed there).  Line 34 prints
!                    000000.40, 0o40 = 32 -- but LV swallows the
!                    bits below the half word (measured), so this
!                    row pins S QK only to 32..63 and the value
!                    comes from p.109, not from here.
SQK     SYN(BU,18), .32
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! RECORDED AND NOT EXPLAINED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A BARE "*" AFTER THE LOCATION on lines 1, 19 and 37 --
! "217245.00 *", "217260.40 *", "217274.00 *".  printed pp.3, 37,
! 103, 120, 128 and 136 carry the same mark and it was left
! unexplained on each; the volume OCR of printed p.143 marks ITS
! line 1 the same way.  It changes no compiled bit.  Note that line
! 37 is a verbatim repeat of line 29 ("T,15,SLRBU,SLRPP" against
! "T,$15,SLRBU,SLRPP") and only one of the two is starred, so it is
! not a property of the statement.
!
! THE PAGE PRINTS THE SAME THREE-ROW SEQUENCE THREE TIMES with the
! register written "$15" once and "15" twice (lines 28/29 against
! 36/37 and 41 following), and the deck transcribes each as printed.
! Both forms compile identically, which is itself worth recording:
! "LCI,$15,30.0" and "LCI,15,30" both give 000036.37 02.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! COVERAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ALL FIFTY-TWO EMITTING ROWS CARRY A !CHECK and all six symbols a
! !SYM.  Lines 52-55 have no !CHECK because they are comment cards
! and emit nothing.  Fifty-one of the fifty-two checks are on the
! printed statement exactly as it stands; line 4 is the one
! SUBSTITUTION and is flagged above and in its own !CHECK note.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

        SLC, (8)217245.0

        LV,$0,$L                        ! line  1
        V+,$0,$0                        ! line  2
        LC,$0,$0                        ! line  3  -N IN $0
        M-(BU,19),MPRMQK,-19            ! line  4  printed form, no substitution
        LX,$3,MR5                       ! line  5  -TRANSMIT CONTROL
        CM1111(BU,1),.4($2)             ! line  6  -SET USER TO MCP
        SV,$2,MCR                       ! line  7  -SET K IN MCR
        SV,$2,MR3AD                     ! line  8
        Z,1.0($2)                       ! line  9
        V+I,$2,2.32                     ! line 10
MUP5A   L(V+ICR)(BU,32),.32($3)         ! line 11
        ST(V+I)(BU,32),.32($2)          ! line 12  -PARAM. TO TENT.
        CB,$0,MUP5A                     ! line 13  -PARAM FINISHED
        SX,$3,MR5                       ! line 14  -SAVE UNPRIME CONTROL
        B,MTC1                          ! line 15  -ENTER
MB1     M-1(BU,19),STIC                 ! line 16
        B,KSUPP                         ! line 17
MPP1    Z,MCR                           ! line 18
        V-I,9,1.0                       ! line 19
        SIC,JMPP2                       ! line 20
        B,JMPP1                         ! line 21  -CHECK FOR OP, AD, USA, DS
        BB,SAS($9),CRETBU               ! line 22  -RETURN TO PP IF HE IS AUTO STACKED
